# **The gauntlet's work order.** One line per violation, as
# `room | rule | offender` — see `gauntlet.rs`, "The docket".
#
# This file is the deliverable of the harness pass and the input to the
# fixing pass. Strike a line, run `cargo test -p cabin`, and
# `the_gauntlet_finds_exactly_the_docket` will tell you whether the thing
# is actually gone: a line struck too early fails, and a defect fixed
# without striking its line fails too.
#
# Regenerate wholesale with:
#   ./target/debug/space-trucking --gauntlet-docket
# and read the numbers behind any line with:
#   ./target/debug/space-trucking --gauntlet
#
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# **The rooms are clear, the doorways are clear, and these two are what
# is left of the cargo.**
#
# The rooms' own lines were three families and one cause, and they came
# off when a calling room got a deck of its own to lend (`Tile::Staging`,
# docs/ROOMS.md); that history is in the git log and the sentences it
# closed are kept said as tests in `gauntlet.rs`.
#
# The doorways were the third layer, and they went the way the cargo did.
# Every piece of hardware in a seam was built straight into the world, so
# the sweep walked through a dozen doorways a room without being able to
# name one thing in any of them — which is how a latch came to be drawn
# twice at one transform and to photograph two ways. A doorway describes
# itself now (`room::seam_parts`) and is swept from both of its sides,
# because a seam is drawn once by the room with the lower id and stands
# on the boundary both of them own. Fifty-three fights came out of that
# first pass and all fifty-three were cured, in the same three idioms the
# cargo's were: a body written down twice (the latch, the jamb lamp, and
# a corner cell's tread laid once per doorway instead of once per cell);
# two members of one fitting cut to one length so they cross (the lintel
# against both stiles, the hatch coaming against itself at four corners);
# and a part run out flush with the edge its parent was cut at (the frame
# and the coaming against the very plane the aperture was punched on,
# cured by straddling it — half a jamb over the line, which is what a
# lining is for).
#
# The cargo was the second layer. Thirty-two kinds had never been swept
# at all, because a rig was built straight into a live world and there was
# nothing to measure; there is a description now (`pieces::parts`), and
# the sweep found sixty-one things in it. Fifty-nine were fixed where they
# stood and were all three idioms:
#
#   - two members of one fitting cut to one depth, so they share a plane
#     wherever they cross — the window family's four lips and its
#     mullion, the painting's frame, the suspicious crate's hum edges,
#     the mysterious crate's twine, the cabinet's rack and carcass, the
#     chart tank's chassis, and both legs of the gas canister's chevrons;
#   - a part run out flush with its parent's own edge — the cabinet's
#     sides and caps against its back sheet, the chart tank's posts and
#     caps against its plinth, the couch's seat against its backrest;
#   - a part begun on the plane its neighbour begins on — the Guild
#     chit's stripe and the gilded idol's belt, both on their own backs.
#
# The chit is the one the owner found by eye. Its top and bottom edges
# were cured in an earlier pass and its BACK was not, which is the whole
# argument for a harness: an eye finds the fight it is looking at.
#
# The two below are the ones a fix would have to re-draw a kind for, and
# they are the same question asked twice: `pieces::RIG_NEAR..RIG_FAR` is
# the depth every rig is composed within and the depth a berth's air is
# measured over, and these two parts are outside it. The floor lamp's
# base disc is a hand's breadth wider than the pole it carries and lies
# behind the berth plane; the very mysterious crate's core hangs proud of
# a crate that already fills the band. Either the parts move or the band
# is two numbers too tight — and while it stands, every berth those two
# kinds take is measured shallower than the thing standing in it.

# ---- rigs ----
rigs | berth-clear | FloorLamp base plate
rigs | berth-clear | VeryMysteriousCrate core
